course: dictionary
lesson: 15503
title: Divide, then divide again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To divide something is to split it into parts. To subdivide it is to split it again, so the parts get smaller. The prefix sub- means under or within, so subdivide is a second, smaller division.
explain: «We cut the pizza into halves. Then we subdivided each half into quarters.» The halves were already divided, so subdivided means split again into smaller parts. Check your meaning in the sentence: «split the parts again» still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: Some words in this family grow from it. «The farmer decided to subdivide the large field into small plots for new houses.» Here subdivide is about land. A subdivision is a new housing area made this way, and people often use this sense in the USA, Canada, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: To subdivide means to divide something that is already divided into even smaller parts.
fact: To subdivide land means to split a big piece of land into smaller plots for houses.
fact: In maths, you can subdivide a number line into tenths, or a half into quarters.
fact: In science, a large group of animals is subdivided into smaller groups such as families.
exercise: «We cut the pizza into halves, then subdivided each half into quarters.» What does subdivided mean here? | Eaten all at once | *Divided again into smaller parts | Thrown away | Joined together
exercise: «The council plans to subdivide the large farm into small plots for new homes.» What is being subdivided? | *A large piece of land | A river | A school | A lake
exercise: «In science, a large group of animals is subdivided into smaller groups, such as families.» Which word names one of those smaller groups? | Ocean | Pencil | Cloud | *Family
test: «Each tenth on the number line was subdivided into ten smaller marks.» What does subdivided mean? | Measured in metres | Painted in red | *Split into smaller parts again | Removed from the line
test: Which word names a new housing area made by subdividing land? | Subway | Subtraction | *Subdivision | Submarine
exam: «The teacher asked us to subdivide each group of animals into smaller groups.» What did the teacher ask us to do? | Name the animals in each group | *Split each group into smaller groups | Make the groups bigger | Count each animal only once
